# Ansible Linux Infrastructure Automation

A hands-on DevOps project for automating the configuration and management of multiple Ubuntu servers using Ansible.

The project starts from basic SSH connectivity and inventory management and evolves into a role-based Ansible structure for server baseline configuration, user management, Nginx deployment, SSH access management, firewall configuration, and service verification.

## Architecture

```text
                    Ansible Control Node
                            |
                            | SSH
                    User: ansible
                            |
                 +----------+----------+
                 |                     |
                 v                     v
               web01                 web02
           192.168.1.20          192.168.1.30
                 |                     |
              Ubuntu                 Ubuntu
                 |                     |
               Nginx                 Nginx
```

Ansible connects to the Managed Nodes using SSH public-key authentication.

Privileged tasks use:

```yaml
become: true
```

so Ansible connects as the non-root `ansible` user and uses `sudo` when administrative privileges are required.

