## Jinja2 Templates

Nginx configuration and HTML pages are generated dynamically using Jinja2.

Example:

```nginx
listen {{ nginx_port }};
root {{ nginx_web_root }};
```

Host-specific information is also rendered using Ansible Facts and inventory variables.

For example:

```html
<p>Server: {{ inventory_hostname }}</p>
<p>System Hostname: {{ ansible_hostname }}</p>
<p>Environment: {{ lab_environment }}</p>
```

The same template therefore produces different output for `web01` and `web02`.

---

## Handlers

Nginx is reloaded only when its configuration actually changes.

Flow:

```text
Template changed
       ↓
notify
       ↓
nginx -t
       ↓
configuration valid
       ↓
Reload Nginx
```

If no configuration change occurs, the handler is not triggered.

---

## Idempotency

The playbooks describe the desired state rather than repeatedly executing shell commands.

After the infrastructure reaches the required state, running the same playbook again should result in approximately:

```text
changed=0
failed=0
unreachable=0
```

This demonstrates Ansible idempotency.

